\f0\fs24 \cf0 Here\'92s a concise overview based on available results:\
\
- How many Rincon Clubhouses in Panama: Eight Rincones in the country as of 2023, with more recent additions like a new site at the Panama American Center in 2026. [senacyt.gob](https://www.senacyt.gob.pa/la-red-nacional-de-rincones-clubhouse-celebro-su-segundo-aniversario-ensenando-tecnologia-a-la-juventud-panamena/)\
- When it began: The Clubhouse Network started in 1993; Panama joined the initiative in 2004 with two early centers (Parroquia de F\'e1tima in Chorrillo and Fe y Alegr\'eda in El Ingenio). The Panamanian national network then expanded to eight Rincones. [senacyt.gob](https://www.senacyt.gob.pa/la-red-nacional-de-rincones-clubhouse-celebro-su-segundo-aniversario-ensenando-tecnologia-a-la-juventud-panamena/)\
- Who funds it: The program is an initiative of SENACYT (Secretar\'eda Nacional de Ciencia, Tecnolog\'eda e Innovaci\'f3n) in Panama, funded and managed through its Directorate of Innovation in Learning, with partnerships (e.g., The Clubhouse Network, U.S. actors) for implementation and support. [senacyt.gob](https://www.senacyt.gob.pa/la-red-nacional-de-rincones-clubhouse-celebro-su-segundo-aniversario-ensenando-tecnologia-a-la-juventud-panamena/)\
- What is its purpose: To provide free, after-school learning spaces that use technology to foster creativity, autonomy, confidence, and project-based learning among youth, especially in socially vulnerable regions. It follows The Clubhouse Network model emphasizing learning by doing, interest-driven projects, community, and mentorship. [senacyt.gob](https://www.senacyt.gob.pa/la-red-nacional-de-rincones-clubhouse-celebro-su-segundo-aniversario-ensenando-tecnologia-a-la-juventud-panamena/)\
- History/highlights:\
  - Origin: Panamanian entry in 2004 with two centers; growth to eight Rincones nationwide. [senacyt.gob](https://www.senacyt.gob.pa/la-red-nacional-de-rincones-clubhouse-celebro-su-segundo-aniversario-ensenando-tecnologia-a-la-juventud-panamena/)\
  - 2023: National network celebrated its second anniversary, highlighting expansion and impact on youth technology learning. [senacyt.gob](https://www.senacyt.gob.pa/la-red-nacional-de-rincones-clubhouse-celebro-su-segundo-aniversario-ensenando-tecnologia-a-la-juventud-panamena/)\
  - 2026: U.S. Embassy and SENACYT launched a new Rincon Clubhouse at the Panama American Center in Ciudad del Saber, expanding STEAM learning space for ages 12\'9617. [pa.usembassy](https://pa.usembassy.gov/u-s-embassy-ciudad-del-saber-and-senacyt-launch-rincon-clubhouse-at-the-panama-american-center/)\
